{
  "id": "rways_souss",
  "name": "Rrways (Souss Amazigh troubadour song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Professional song of Tashelhit-speaking Amazigh troupes of the Souss in southern Morocco, each led by a rais (poet-singer) who composes and sings with musicians and dancers at festivals, weddings and markets. Hadj Belaid recorded rrways songs for 78 rpm labels in the 1930s, and later raises and raissas made it a large cassette repertoire. The rabab_maghribi card stands in for the single-string Amazigh ribab, and the anvil card in its brake-drum form for the naqus, a piece of metal struck with iron rods; the troupe's lotar lutes have no card.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1930s rrways, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. single leader group response, single lead single track no stacking. rabab maghribi, brake drum metal beater anvil. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
